# Files whose BYTES are evidence, marked so git never rewrites a line ending in
# them on checkout or on commit.
#
# docs/lessons/operations.md (OPS-20260914-LEDGERCRLF) states the rule: the scope
# is any tracked file whose bytes are evidence. Two such files exist today.
#
#   src/minireason/loop/data/**   the standard's shipped data. Their sha256 is
#                                 pinned into `loop_plan_id` by
#                                 minireason.loop.standard (CEILING_SHA256 and,
#                                 through the ceiling digest, STANDARD_BODY_SHA256).
#                                 A CRLF checkout changes both digests while every
#                                 required sentence still parses -- text-mode
#                                 universal newlines hide it -- so the plan identity
#                                 would move and nothing would say so.
#   docs/DECISION_LEDGER.md       append-only, and already carries CRLF lines from
#                                 earlier publishers. `-text` keeps them exactly as
#                                 they are; the ledger writer only ever appends.
#
# There is deliberately NO global `* text=auto eol=lf` line. This repository
# carries historical CRLF bytes in tracked files, and a global rule would renormalise
# them on the next checkout -- a large diff of files nobody edited, which is noise in
# front of the two files that actually matter here.

src/minireason/loop/data/** -text
docs/DECISION_LEDGER.md -text
